   "sentenceId": 6,
   "he": "מַתְנִי׳ הָאוֹמֵר ״בְּנִי זֶה מַמְזֵר״ – אֵינוֹ נֶאֱמָן. וַאֲפִילּוּ שְׁנֵיהֶם מוֹדִים עַל הָעוּבָּר שֶׁבְּמֵעֶיהָ מַמְזֵר הוּא – אֵינָם נֶאֱמָנִים. רַבִּי יְהוּדָה אוֹמֵר: נֶאֱמָנִים.",
   "en": "«MISHNA:» «One who says: This son of mine» is «a mamzer,» e.g., if he claims that the son was born to one forbidden to him by a prohibition that carries the punishment of karet, «he is not deemed credible» to render him a mamzer. «And even» if «both of them,» the father and the mother, «admit that a fetus in her womb is a mamzer, they are not deemed credible. Rabbi Yehuda says: They are deemed credible.»"
  }
 ],
